 *   **Performance:** Adds negligible computational overhead compared to the table lookup. However, it increases implementation complexity [S6, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Simple to implement; resolves the most common face-level topological errors; ensures continuity across shared faces between adjacent cubes.
-*   **Limitations:** Does not resolve interior ambiguities (tunnels). Requires scalar values at vertices (not just binary occupancy).
