 ## Background
-The Asymptotic Decider was proposed by Nielson and Hamann in 1991 [S1][S2][S5, unofficial]. It was introduced to address the ambiguities in the original Marching Cubes algorithm identified by Dürst and others, specifically regarding the behavior of the trilinear interpolant on cube faces [S1][S2]. The method was published in "The Asymptotic Decider: Resolving the Ambiguity in Marching Cubes" [S5, unofficial]. It was later observed by Natarajan (1994) that similar ambiguities exist in the interior of the cube, leading to further extensions like Marching Cubes 33 [S2][S8].
